# Admin panel for new features

When adding a feature that operators might want to configure, toggle, or inspect, expose it on `/admin` in the same change — do not leave it hardcoded or view-only unless it is intentionally guest-facing only.

## What belongs in admin

- Slideshow behaviour (duration, transitions, queue rules, captions)
- Upload/processing options that affect the event (limits, compression, moderation)
- Anything stored in `data/state.json` or similar shared config

## What usually does not

- Pure guest UX polish on `/upload` with no operator knob
- One-off bug fixes with no new setting

## How to wire it

1. Persist config in state (or env only if truly deploy-time).
2. Add/extend admin API under `/api/admin/...` with `require_admin`.
3. Add UI in `templates/admin.html` + `static/admin.js`, matching existing panels.
4. Have `/view` (and related clients) read the setting from the API/config response.

```text
❌ BAD: hardcode transition list only in view.js with no admin control
✅ GOOD: store enabled transitions / mode in state; admin toggles; /view consumes config
```
